# UIAnchor

**Full guidelines:** [docs/UIANCHOR_GUIDELINES.md](docs/UIANCHOR_GUIDELINES.md) — follow that doc for naming, when to anchor, Playwright usage, PR checklist, and deferred features. This rule is a short reminder; the guidelines file is the source of truth.

Stable UI identity shared by app code and Playwright. Contract: `data-ui="<identity>"`. Helpers: `@/lib/uianchor` · `ui()` in `e2e/fixtures.ts`.

## When to anchor

Anchor only what E2E will click, fill, or assert: form fields/submit, primary nav/logout, page landmarks, list static actions. Do not anchor layout/decoration or icon-only children of an already-anchored control.

## Contract

One component declaration → one identity → one `data-ui` → one Playwright `ui()` locator. App owns the identity; tests consume it. Never invent IDs only in tests. Prefer `data-ui` over `data-testid` for new anchors.

```tsx
import { Anchor } from "@/lib/uianchor";
<Anchor.Input ui="auth.login.email" id="login-email" type="email" />
<Anchor.Button ui="auth.login.submit" type="submit">Sign In</Anchor.Button>
```

- `ui` → `data-ui` (identity). Keep native HTML `id` for a11y/labels — never put the UIAnchor identity in HTML `id`.
- Landmarks may use raw `data-ui` on a plain element.
- Primitives: `Anchor.Button` · `Anchor.Input` · `Anchor.Select` · `Anchor.Link`.

## Naming

Format: `<domain>.<area>.<element>[.<action>]` — lowercase, dot-separated, ≥2 segments, each `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*`. Describe what, not how.

Prefixes: `auth.*` · `public.*` · `shared.*` · `superadmin.*` · `hospitaladmin.*` · `doctor.*` · `staff.*` · `receptionist.*` · `finance.*` · `parentdept.*` · `subdept.*` (type suffix when needed) · `clinical.*` / `diagnostic.*` / `administrative.*` / `support.*`.

Prefer portal-scoped IDs for shell chrome. Shared panels: pass `uiPrefix` (preferred) or use `shared.*` only when meaning is identical everywhere.

## Playwright

```ts
import { test, expect } from "./fixtures";
await ui("auth.login.email").fill("…");
await ui("auth.login.submit").click();
await expect(ui("hospitaladmin.dashboard")).toBeVisible();
```

No new CSS/text/nth-child selectors for controls that have (or should have) a UIAnchor. Use Playwright built-ins only.

## Generated inventory

After adding/changing anchors, run `npm run uianchor:generate` (also runs on `pretypecheck`).

- Manifest: `src/lib/uianchor/ui-anchor.manifest.json`
- Typed union: `src/lib/uianchor/ids.generated.ts` (`UIAnchorId`)
- Playwright `ui()` is typed with `UIAnchorId` — never hand-edit generated files or invent IDs only in tests

## Do not

- Encode CSS/layout into IDs, or derive identity from classes/DOM position/copy/random IDs
- Use array indexes as identity (`row(0)`); instance IDs (`data-ui-instance`) are deferred
- Turn UIAnchor into a framework, assertion library, or hand-written ID inventory
